          deepDive: "**V-る + ことはない** literally says *there is no occasion to ~* → *there's no need to ~, you don't have to ~*. The book stresses its main job: **advice or reassurance** to someone else (アドバイスに使うことが多い): 君が謝ることはないよ。悪いのは向こうなんだから (*there's no need for you to apologize — they're the ones in the wrong*). It's warmer than 〜なくてもいい: the speaker is telling the listener not to trouble themselves.\n\nConnection (the book): dictionary form + **ことはない** or **こともない**. こともない adds *even* (*there isn't even any need to ~*) and sounds a touch softer or more offhand. Polite: ことはありません. Common companions: **わざわざ** (*go out of your way*) — わざわざ買うことはないよ (*no need to go and buy one*); **そんなに**; **〜くらいで** — 虫に刺されたくらいで病院に行くことはない (*no need to go to the hospital over an insect bite*). A reason often follows: 〜んだから, 〜から.\n\nNuance:\n- Said to someone who *has already done* something, it becomes a gentle **reproach**: そんなに笑うことはないでしょう (*you don't have to laugh that much!* — review 問題4-2). Past: 〜ことはなかった (*you didn't need to ~*): 謝ることはなかったのに (*you didn't have to apologize*).\n- It's about **necessity**, not about whether the action happens. 明日行くことはない = *there's no need to go tomorrow*, not *I won't go tomorrow* (行かない).\n- With an uncontrollable event it can simply mean *it never happens*: この地方で雪が降ることはない (*it never snows in this region*). Addressed to a listener about their own action, it's advice.\n\nDon't mix it up with:\n- **V-たことがない**, *have never done* (experience): 謝ったことがない (*I've never apologized*). Note が and the た-form.\n- **〜ないことはない** (#54), *it's not that ~ not*: 心配しないことはない (*it's not that I don't worry*) — two negatives, a grudging yes.\n- **〜ことだ** (#87), *you should ~* — advice TO do something: 早く寝ることだ (*you'd better get to bed early*). ことはない is advice NOT to bother.\n- **〜わけにはいかない** (#57), *can't (for social reasons)*: 休むわけにはいかない (*I can't take the day off*) — an obligation, not freedom from one.\n\nCommon mistake: ✗行かないことはないよ (meant as *no need to go*) → ✓行くことはないよ. The verb stays in the affirmative dictionary form; adding ない turns it into #54.\n\nJLPT tip: look for a reassuring reason (まだ時間はありますから, 大丈夫だから). Review 問題1-4: まだ時間はありますから、急ぐことはありません (*there's still time, so there's no need to hurry*). The distractors どころではありません (#38, *this is no time for ~*), わけにはいきません (*I can't*) and おそれがあります (#34, *there's a risk*) don't follow from a relaxed reason.",
