          deepDive: "**〜ものか** is a **rhetorical question** used as a strong denial: *would I ever ~? — never!* 負けるものか = *am I going to lose? — no way!* It's said with a **falling** intonation; the か doesn't really ask anything. The book gives two uses:\n- **Determination**, often muttered to oneself (独り言): こんなサービスの悪い店には二度と来るもんか (*I'm never coming back to a shop with service this bad*).\n- **Flat rejection** of what someone just said, often echoing their word: A：楽そうね。 B：楽なもんか。1日に何千個も入れるんだよ (*Easy? Not a chance. I have to bag thousands a day*).\nIt also denies that something is possible: あいつがあきらめるものか (*as if that guy would give up*), 経験のないお前にわかるものか (*how could someone with no experience like you understand?*).\n\nConnection (the book): V-る / いA / なA**な** / N**な** + ものか. ✗天才だもんか → ✓天才なもんか (*a genius? hardly*). Forms and register:\n- **もんか** — the usual spoken form (the book: 話し言葉では「〜もんか」「〜もんですか」).\n- **ものか** — a little more formal or written; also in quoted resolutions: 泣くものかという気持ち (*the attitude of \"I won't cry\"*).\n- **ものですか / もんですか** — polite, softer, often heard from women: うそなんかつくもんですか (*why would I lie?*).\n- Typical helpers: 二度と, 絶対, 誰が〜ものか (*who would ever ~?*), 〜なんか.\n\nDon't confuse it with:\n- **〜ことか** (#42), *how ~ it is!* — an exclamation that *affirms*: 何度泣いたことか (*how many times I cried!*). 優しいことか praises; 優しいもんか denies.\n- **〜もん** (#56), a casual *because* — no か: だって、疲れたんだもん (*but I'm tired!*).\n- **〜ものだ** (#13), *that's the nature of ~*: 子どもは騒ぐものだ (*kids are noisy by nature*).\n- **〜ものではない** (#46), *one shouldn't ~* (social advice): 人の悪口を言うものではない (*you shouldn't speak ill of others*).\n- **V-るまい** (#93), written *I will never ~ / surely not*: 二度と行くまい (*I'll never go again*).\n- **〜わけがない** (N3), *there's no way ~* — a reasoned judgment; ものか is emotional.\n\nCommon mistake: it's emotional and confrontational, not a polite refusal. Answering a superior's invitation with 行くもんか means *as if I'd go!* — say 申し訳ありませんが、行けません (*I'm sorry, but I can't go*).\n\nJLPT tip: review 問題1-3: A：加藤君のお父さん、優しそうだよね。 B：優しい（もんか）。いつも怒ってばかりいるよ (*Kind? No way. He's always getting angry*). The next sentence contradicts A, so a denial is needed; ことか, ことだ and ものだ all affirm.",
