          deepDive: "Sentence-final **〜もん** (or **〜もの**) gives a reason — the book: 理由の説明や言い訳 (*an explanation or an excuse*). The tone is a little **self-justifying, pleading or childlike**: *but ~ / well, ~, you know*. It very often pairs with **だって** at the start: だって、この人形もこのお菓子も日本じゃなきゃ買えないんだもん (*but you can't buy these dolls or sweets anywhere but Japan!*).\n\nConnection: plain form + もん (the book); the explanatory **〜んだもん** is extremely common. Nouns and な-adjectives keep だ: 子どもだもん (*I'm just a kid!*), 好きだもん. The ＊ note: polite forms occur too — 自分で計算したほうが早いんですもの (*but it's faster to calculate it myself*, example ④).\n\nRegister and speakers:\n- **もん** is casual: children, young people, women; men use it among close friends, where it can sound cute or sulky.\n- **もの** is used mainly by women (the book) and sounds softer and a bit more refined: 〜ですもの.\n- Never in formal situations or to superiors at work — it sounds like making excuses.\n\nTwo nuances:\n- **Excuse / justification** in answer to a complaint or question: A：なんでメールしたのに返事くれなかったの？ B：だって全然気がつかなかったんだもん (*but I didn't notice it at all!*).\n- **A reason shared with the listener**, often with ね: あのミュージカル、人気あるもんね (*well, that musical is popular, after all*); or backing up one's own claim: まだ問題がたくさんあるもん (*there are still lots of problems, you know*).\n\nDon't confuse it with:\n- **〜ものか / もんか** (#51), *no way!*: 行くもんか (*as if I'd go!*). Only the か differs, but it's a strong denial.\n- **〜もので / もんで** (N3), a mid-sentence reason used in apologies: 慣れないもので、ご迷惑をおかけしました (*I'm not used to it, so I've caused you trouble*) — the polite way to make an excuse.\n- **〜ものだ** (#13), *by nature*, and **〜ものだ** (#132), nostalgia: よく遊んだものだ (*we used to play a lot*).\n\nCommon mistake: ✗遅れてすみません。電車が遅れたんだもん (to a boss) → ✓電車が遅れたもので (*the train was delayed, you see*).\n\nJLPT tip: in 即時応答 listening, a reply starting だって…んだもん answers a complaint or reproach with a justification that must actually explain it. Review 問題4-2: A：そんなに笑うことはないでしょう。 B：だって、変な格好してるんだもん (*but you're dressed so weirdly!*). 悲しい or おもしろくない can't justify laughing.",
