          deepDive: "The N4 **つもり** is *intention*: V-るつもりだ (*I intend to ~*). This point is different: **V-たつもりで / Nのつもりで** = *in the frame of mind that ~, as if ~*. The book: 本当はそうではないが、そのような気持ちになって — it isn't really so, but you put yourself in that frame of mind: 旅行に行ったつもりで、この「列車の旅」のDVDを見て楽しみましょう (*let's enjoy this \"Train Journey\" DVD and imagine we've gone on a trip*). The speaker knows it's make-believe and chooses that attitude, usually to do something better or enjoy it more.\n\nConnection (the book): **V-た**, **いA**, **なA + な**, **N + の** + つもり(で): 行ったつもり, 若いつもり, 元気なつもり, 家族のつもり.\n\nCommon shapes:\n- **〜になったつもりで** — role-play: 政治家になったつもりで討論しましょう (*let's debate as if we were politicians*, the Check); レポーターになったつもりで人の話をよく聞き (*listen carefully to people as if you were a reporter*, review 問題2).\n- **本番／試合のつもりで** — treat practice as the real thing: 練習のときは試合のつもりで気合を入れて (*in practice, go all out as if it were a real match*).\n- **〜たつもりで貯金する** — the classic saving trick: 買ったつもりで貯金する (*put the money in savings as if you'd bought it*).\n- With いA it can be critical: いつまでも若いつもりで徹夜してると体を壊すよ (*if you keep pulling all-nighters, thinking you're as young as ever, you'll ruin your health*).\n\nDon't confuse it with:\n- **〜つもり（だ）** (#120), *I believe I did ~ (but actually…)*: 鍵をかけたつもりだったのに、開いていた (*I thought I'd locked it, but it was open*). In #120 the speaker genuinely believes it; here the speaker knows it's pretend.\n- **〜ふりをする**, *pretend (to others)*: 寝ているふりをする (*pretend to be asleep*) — an outward act to fool someone. つもりで is an inner frame of mind, usually for motivation.\n- **まるで〜ように**, *just as if*: describes how something looks, not a chosen attitude: まるで夢のようだ (*it's just like a dream*).\n\nCommon mistake: using V-る. ✗旅行に行くつもりでDVDを見る means *I watch the DVD intending to go on a trip*. For *as if*, use the past: 行ったつもりで.\n\nJLPT tip: in 問題2, つもりで usually follows 〜になった and is followed by the action done in that spirit: レポーターに／なった／つもりで／人の話をよく聞き.",
